# Profile Evolution Candidate Review Specialization

Status: NON_AUTHORITY_CANDIDATE / INERT UNTIL ADMISSION

## Purpose
When Quality Pack is asked to independently review a Profile Evolution candidate, evaluate whether the claimed specialization or adaptation is supported by exact evidence rather than by structural compatibility alone.

## Required candidate evidence
- exact baseline profile revision and target identity;
- evolution mode and evidence-bound PROFILE_ASSESSMENT result;
- explicit evidence map for each claimed capability gap or uplift;
- preservation constraints for existing profile responsibilities;
- reversible candidate/materialization receipt;
- benchmark/holdout evidence when capability uplift is claimed;
- independent assurance evidence before any admission claim.

## Fail-closed rules
Return the candidate for repair or additional evidence when maturity is inferred from UNKNOWN evidence, structural compatibility is presented as capability maturity, benchmark or holdout evidence is missing for an uplift claim, preservation constraints are absent, or the candidate attempts to self-authorize write/runtime/production impact.

## Boundary
This specialization does not admit, merge, promote, activate or write a profile. It only extends Quality Pack review criteria for Profile Evolution candidates after the normal resolver-backed evidence boundary has been satisfied.
